# orca-wrapper reverse proxy -- public HTTPS entry for the PR-comment wrapper.
#
# Plain HTTP is forbidden here on purpose: ORCA_WRAPPER_TOKEN is a static
# bearer token sent on every request (from the GitHub Actions workflow and by
# hand for debugging). Over cleartext HTTP it travels in the open -- anyone on
# the network path (wifi, a transparent proxy, the cloud network fabric) can
# read it, then call the wrapper's endpoints directly. That is remote code
# execution against the Orca desktop sitting behind it. Caddy auto-provisions
# a Let's Encrypt cert for this domain and redirects HTTP -> HTTPS by default
# -- do not add a `http://` site block or `auto_https off` to this file.
orca.shouttgt.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787

	log {
		output file /var/log/caddy/orca.log
	}
}
